# The playground's endpoints. The API panel sends these (so do VS Code's REST Client and
# JetBrains' HTTP Client), and paths are relative to the server, which listens on the port
# it prints (the workspace's PORT). The > lines say what each request should get back.

### Say hello
GET /api/hello?name=Ana

> status 200
> json $ == {"message": "Hello, Ana!"}

### Without a name
GET /api/hello

> status 200
> json $.message == "Hello, World!"

### A name that is too long answers 400, as an RFC 9457 problem
GET /api/hello?name=Bartholomew-Maximilian-Fitzgerald-Jones-the-Third

> status 400
> header Content-Type ~ ^application/problem\+json
> json $.title == "Bad Request"

### Is the app up? Actuator answers this one
GET /actuator/health

> status 200
> json $.status == "UP"
